Renames a node in your network

Usage: headscale nodes rename [OPTIONS] <NEW_NAME_OR_ID> [HOSTNAME]

Arguments:
  <NEW_NAME_OR_ID>  New hostname in upstream form, or node ID in legacy positional form
  [HOSTNAME]        New hostname when using the legacy `rename ID HOSTNAME` form

Options:
  -c, --config <CONFIG>  config file (default is /etc/headscale/config.yaml) [env: HEADSCALE_CONFIG=]
  -i, --identifier <ID>  Node identifier (ID)
  -o, --output <OUTPUT>  Output format. Empty for human-readable, 'json', 'json-line' or 'yaml'
      --force            Disable prompts and forces the execution
  -h, --help             Print help
